>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Elim`

``` hol4
clasetLib.Elim : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as an unsafe elimination rule for one tactic invocation.

`Elim th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but a classical tactic recognizes
its marker and adds `th` to the call's temporary rule set. An elimination
rule matches its major premise against an assumption and its conclusion
against the goal. It is classified as unsafe for proof search.

The safe classical tactics do not apply unsafe rules. Use `SElim th` to make a
rule available to `SAFE_TAC`, `CLARIFY_TAC`, and their safe step variants.
The `[elim]` theorem attribute persistently registers an unsafe elimination
rule and optionally accepts an Aesop success percentage, as in
`[elim=75]`; `[selim]` registers a safe one.

### Failure

Constructing `Elim th` does not validate the rule. A tactic that consumes
the marker may fail if `th` has no suitable major premise or cannot be
converted to elimination-rule form.

### Example

This accepts `my_elim` into the temporary rule set but does not make it a
safe rule:

``` hol4
classicalLib.SAFE_TAC [clasetLib.Elim my_elim]
```

